Z||000004||starfighter007@msn.com||08-11-2001||12:21 PM||||I would not flush the system out with anything other then pure water.why you ask?Well I will tell you .A few months back I flushed out my cooling system with Radiator flush.It did such a great job that it caused water pump to leak at the seal,head gaskets to leak. what seemed like a good idea turned out to be tragic for me.Just my two cents.goodluck||||reg||11
Z||000005||theogre||08-11-2001||01:25 PM||||Flushing products have to be selected very carefully. Never use an Acid flush in Fiero.<P>Fiero uses an Aliminum Radiator with plastic tanks and a soldered brass heater core.<P>The General Concensus in the industry is the OAT(Organic Acid Technology) products like DEX-COOL(R) and HOAT(Hybrid Organic Acid Technology) used by Ford & Chrysler Should Not be used in older systems. While it may not cause any harm to convert, you would then face the same issues as factory cars that come with it. <P>I have still not gotten a current and difinitve answer on converting. Most documents I've found are a couple years old. The last thing I can find from GM states that when DEX-COOL is used in vehicles built before the intorduction of DEX-COOL, the service interval shall remain the same. They don't say that it will hurt anyhting.<P>Any one with cars that came with DEX-COOL should read the IMCOOL article linked in my cave. It explains allot of why there are problems showing up with the product. While DEX-COOL has an excelent service life, there are rules to be followed with it or you'll have sludge problems and other issues.||||reg||1
